  "out_of_scope_notes": "Nice classes overlap: a supplement brand routinely files in 29 and 30 alongside 5, and its goods text then trips food keywords such as 'honey', 'spreads' or 'protein'. Class membership therefore cannot decide what the product is. These groups are matched against the goods/services text and win when they dominate it, or when a single unambiguous marker appears alongside the pharmaceutical class. Records they claim are classified out of scope and suppressed from LaunchTrace Food rather than being given a packaged-food category they do not belong in. LaunchTrace Food is not a supplements feed.",
